            "path": "/memories/session/kit-diagram-selection-findings.md",
            "file_text": "# Kit App Diagram and Selection Handling - Analysis\n\n## Test Failure Context\n- Test file: [sketchpad.test.ts](sketchpad.test.ts#L1630)\n- Line 1630: Clicks a `.react-flow__node` and expects selection to contain `types` or `designs`\n- **Actual result**: Selection only contains `folders` (incorrect)\n- **Expected result**: Selection should contain `types` or `designs`\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. Selection State Type - KitAppSelection\n**File**: [Kit.tsx](Kit.tsx#L293-306)\n**Lines**: 293-306\n\n```typescript\nexport interface KitAppSelection {\n  types?: Guid[];           // Selected types\n  designs?: Guid[];         // Selected designs\n  qualities?: string[];\n  ports?: Guid[];\n  tags?: Guid[];\n  concepts?: Guid[];\n  files?: string[];\n  folders?: Guid[];         // \u003c-- Currently being set instead of types/designs\n  authors?: string[];\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Node Click Handler - onSelectionChange\n**File**: [Kit.tsx](Kit.tsx#L8020-8054)\n**Lines**: 8020-8054\n\nThe handler parses node.id in format `\"kind:guid\"`:\n```typescript\nconst onSelectionChange = useCallback(\n  ({ nodes: selectedNodes }: any) =\u003e {\n    const newSelection: KitAppSelection = {};\n    selectedNodes.forEach((node: any) =\u003e {\n      const [kind, guid] = node.id.split(\":\");\n      if (kind === \"type\") {\n        if (!newSelection.types) newSelection.types = [];\n        newSelection.types.push(guid);\n      } else if (kind === \"design\") {\n        if (!newSelection.designs) newSelection.designs = [];\n        newSelection.designs.push(guid);\n      } else if (kind === \"folder\") {\n        if (!newSelection.folders) newSelection.folders = [];\n        newSelection.folders.push(guid);\n      }\n      // ... other kinds\n    });\n    actor.send({ type: \"KIT.SET_SELECTION\", kitGuid, selection: newSelection });\n  },\n  [actor, kitGuid],\n);\n```\n\n### 3. Diagram Node Creation - buildKitDiagramData\n**File**: [Kit.tsx](Kit.tsx#L7349-7550)\n**Lines**: 7349-7550\n\nThe node ID format is created as:\n```typescript\nconst nodeId = `${kind}:${item.guid}`;\n```\n\nWhere `kind` values are from:\n```typescript\nconst kindGroups: KitDiagramNodeKind[] = [\"type\", \"design\", \"quality\", \"port\", \"tag\", \"concept\", \"file\", \"folder\", \"author\"];\n```\n\nNodes are created with:\n```typescript\nnodes.push({\n  id: nodeId,              // e.g., \"type:abc123\" or \"design:xyz789\"\n  type: \"artifact\",\n  position: { x: 0, y: 0 },\n  width: frame.width,\n  height: frame.height,\n  data: {\n    guid: item.guid,\n    name: item.name,\n    kind,                  // \"type\" | \"design\" | \"folder\" etc.\n    icon: item.icon,\n    parentGuid: item.parentGuid,\n    concepts: item.concepts,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### 4. KitDiagramNodeKind Type\n**Files**: \n- [kitSelectionHelpers.ts](kitSelectionHelpers.ts#L217)\n- [kitSelectionHelper.ts](kitSelectionHelper.ts#L182)\n\n```typescript\nexport type KitDiagramNodeKind = \"type\" | \"design\" | \"quality\" | \"port\" | \"tag\" | \"concept\" | \"file\" | \"folder\" | \"author\";\n```\n\n### 5. KitDiagramNode Interface\n**File**: [Kit.tsx](Kit.tsx#L6995-7006)\n\n```typescript\ninterface KitDiagramNode extends Record\u003cstring, unknown\u003e {\n  guid: string;\n  name: string;\n  kind: KitDiagramNodeKind;\n  icon?: string | React.ReactNode;\n  parentGuid?: string;\n  concepts?: string[];\n}\n```\n\n## Problem Analysis\n\nThe test is clicking nodes and expecting `types` or `designs` in the selection, but getting `folders` instead. This suggests:\n\n1. **Possible causes**:\n   - The clicked node's ID might be parsing incorrectly (e.g., node.id format is wrong)\n   - The node.id might contain \"folder:\" prefix when it should be \"type:\" or \"design:\"\n   - The buildKitDiagramData function might be creating folder nodes instead of type/design nodes\n   - The test might be clicking the wrong nodes\n\n2. **Debug needs**:\n   - Check what node types are actually being rendered in the diagram\n   - Verify the node.id values being sent to onSelectionChange\n   - Check the kit data being passed to buildKitDiagramData (does it have types/designs?)\n"
